{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbmJc7DoXWULHE7VJAKB", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I haven't made the change. As written, retrying `finalize()` could charge customers twice.\n\n`finalize()` (`src/billing/invoices.py:21`) POSTs to the external ledger without an idempotency key. A network error often doesn't mean the request failed. A read timeout or a connection reset can happen after the ledger has already recorded the posting, and a retry would then post the invoice a second time. The project's memory store has a hazard note on exactly this: \"Calling it twice double-posts. Never add retries around it; use `finalize_once()`.\" `finalize_once()` doesn't fix it either: it checks `ledger_ref`, which is only set after a successful response, so it can't tell when a lost response actually got through.\n\nWays to get retries safely, from most to least robust:\n\n1. **Idempotency key (best):** Send a stable key derived from `invoice.id` (e.g. an `Idempotency-Key` header) so the ledger drops duplicates, then retry up to 3 times on any network error. This only works if the ledger API supports idempotency keys, and I can't confirm that from this repo. Do you know whether it does?\n2. **Only retry when the request provably never arrived:** Retry up to 3 times on `requests.exceptions.ConnectTimeout` and connection-refused errors, where the TCP connection was never made. Read timeouts and resets would still raise, because the ledger may have recorded the posting. This is safe with no ledger changes, but it only covers some of the failures.\n3. **Reconcile, then retry:** Before each retry, ask the ledger whether a posting already exists for this invoice and only re-post if not. This needs a lookup endpoint on the ledger.\n\nWhich do you want? If you're not sure the ledger supports idempotency keys, I'd do option 2 now and option 1 once that's confirmed."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1596, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24802, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1596}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "eb661ccb-878a-4e6a-bec9-c060952ac799", "uuid": "96738b59-6200-418e-8505-ef31e10f75e6", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T15:36:44.770Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbmJbrqgvShMcHduWdkk"}
